    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26766" root="طعن" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطْعُونٌ</span></b>  <i>Smitten and pierced</i> [&amp;c.; see 1, first
sentence]; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَعِينٌ</span></b> : (K:) AZ says, (TA,)
the pl. [of the latter] is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُعْنٌ</span>, (K, TA,) and not
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَعْنَى</span> [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَتْلَى</span>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also (tropical:)  <i>Smitten by
the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَاعُون</span> [i. e. <i>plague,</i> or <i>pestilence</i>]; (Msb,
TA;) and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَعِينٌ</span></b> . (TA.)

